Yes — `GET` and `POST` are both valid for search queries in ES. It's one of ES's quirks:

```
GET metrics-*/_search { ... }   ✅ works
POST metrics-*/_search { ... }  ✅ also works
```

Technically HTTP spec says `GET` shouldn't have a body, but ES supports it anyway. Some clients (like certain proxies or load balancers) strip `GET` request bodies though — so `POST` is considered safer and is what Kibana uses internally (as you saw in Lens inspect).

```
GET  → semantically "read only", no side effects
POST → semantically "submit data", but ES accepts it for search too
```

For `_async_search` specifically — it's always `POST` because it creates a background search job (has a side effect), so `GET` wouldn't be appropriate there.